+````markdown name=ops/secure_agg/production_mpc/README.md
+```text
+Production MPC integration - reference & checklist
+
+This folder contains reference code and manifests to run a production-style MPC deployment for secure aggregation.
+It is not a drop-in secure implementation: you must perform the steps below and run the audit checklist.
+
+Key principles
+- Use mTLS for all control & data channels between clients and MPC servers.
+- Use threshold secret-sharing (Shamir) or actively secure MPC (CrypTen/PySyft protocols).
+- Ensure data is quantized and chunked/streamed for large models to avoid OOM.
+- Distribute shares across multiple aggregator replicas to avoid single-point-of-trust.
+
+Files:
+- worker.py : CrypTen worker reference (multi-host via torch.distributed env vars)
+- generate_mtls.sh : helper to create mTLS certs for testing (use proper CA in prod)
+- k8s/worker_statefulset.yaml : StatefulSet template for deploying MPC workers
+- tests/test_mpc_integration.py : local multi-process test harness
+- crypto_audit_checklist.md : checklist for cryptographic review & auditor
+
+High-level deploy steps:
+1) Create CA & mTLS certs (use PKI/CA in prod). See generate_mtls.sh for test certs.
+2) Build worker image and deploy as StatefulSet following k8s template.
+3) Configure Service to allow inter-worker communication; set MASTER_ADDR/PORT, WORLD_SIZE, RANK as env vars for pods.
+4) Run integration tests, monitor memory and latency, evaluate dropout behaviour.
+5) Engage external crypto review.
+
+````

