+````markdown name=ops/secure_agg/production_mpc/crypto_audit_checklist.md
+```text
+Crypto audit checklist for MPC secure-aggregation
+
+1) Threat model & assumptions
+ - Document adversary model: honest-but-curious, malicious clients, malicious aggregator, network attacker.
+ - List trust assumptions and trust boundaries.
+
+2) Protocol selection
+ - Specify chosen MPC protocol (Shamir secret sharing / CrypTen / SPDZ / others).
+ - Provide references to formal definitions and proofs.
+
+3) Implementation review items
+ - Secret-share encoding/decoding correctness & overflow checks.
+ - Quantization & rounding behavior documented with test vectors.
+ - Dropout resilience & threshold handling verification.
+ - Replay protection, nonce usage, and anti-replay measures.
+ - Input validation & size limits.
+
+4) Network & crypto ops
+ - TLS/mTLS configuration & certificate management.
+ - Key handling & rotation for RPC/TLS keys.
+ - Side-channel mitigations (memory cleanup, constant-time ops where applicable).
+
+5) Testing & test vectors
+ - Unit tests reproducing expected outputs for known inputs.
+ - Malicious-share tests (invalid shares, inconsistent sizes).
+ - Performance tests across model sizes & participant counts.
+
+6) Audit & attestation
+ - Provide signed manifests for deployments and test runs.
+ - Record evidence of test runs & signatures in S3/Rekor.
+
+7) Recommendations
+ - Engage third-party cryptographers to validate the code & protocol.
+ - Prefer well-maintained MPC library and avoid ad-hoc implementations.
+
+````

